    priority: 4  # 58b4
    description: "From hg-uat-v4.0.0 directed-validation campaign (2026-05-03), master report\n§ DQ-04 / UX-02. Scope narrowed 2026-05-04 after `hypergumbo run --help`\ninspection — the underlying capability is already there; the gap is purely\ndocumentation.\nMaster report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v4.0.0/lab-notebook/master-report.md\n\n## Original observation\n\n`hypergumbo run --out PATH` writes additional files at the same prefix\nbeyond the requested path:\n\n- `<out_basename>.4k.json` / `.16k.json` / `.64k.json` (compact-tier previews)\n- `slice.handler.index.json`\n- `slice.handler.<METHOD>.<path>.json` (one per detected REST route)\n\nRound 03 (spring-petclinic) saw **30 outputs from a single command**. The\nUAT agent reported this as surprising friction, not knowing that flags to\nsuppress these existed.\n\n## What's already in the CLI\n\n`hypergumbo run --help` already provides opt-out / cap flags for both side-output families:\n\n- `--budgets BUDGETS` — comma-separated specs (`'4k,16k,64k'`), `'default'`,\n  or `'none'` to disable. Controls the compact-tier preview files.\n- `--no-handler-slices` — skip per-route-handler slices entirely.\n- `--max-handler-slices N` — cap the number of slices emitted (default: 25).\n  Overflow handlers are listed in `slice.handler.index.json` for re-derive\n  on demand.\n\nSo **the capability already exists; the discoverability does not**. The\ntop-level `--out OUT` help line reads only \"Output JSON path (default:\n~/.cache/hypergumbo/<repo>/<state>/)\" — nothing in that line tells the\nreader that side-outputs land at the same prefix. The reader has to\nscroll down to `--budgets` and `--no-handler-slices` to learn that.\n\n## Scope (narrowed)\n\nUpdate the `--out OUT` argument's help text in `hypergumbo run`'s argparse\nto call out, at the point of first contact, that the same prefix receives\nadditional files governed by `--budgets` and `--no-handler-slices`. Add\nan example invocation showing how to get exactly one output file:\n\n```\nhypergumbo run . --out analysis.json --budgets none --no-handler-slices\n```\n\n## Out of scope (per 2026-05-04 interview)\n\n- New flags (already exist).\n- Path-layout changes (e.g., sibling `<out>.aux/` directory). The user's\n  steer was \"don't jettison any of those files\" — they're earning their\n  place; the friction is purely awareness.\n- Behavior change of any kind.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n`hypergumbo run --help` output shows, in the `--out OUT` block (not just\nlater in the help), that side-outputs land at the same prefix and points\nat the opt-out flags. The `Examples:` block includes a \"single output file\"\nincantation."  # 58b4
